# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/octo-3 window (octo-T8 and its three levers on the fused stack; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/octo-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-1 is the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (the oneq arm needs its binary; every other arm runs that
# binary with the lever off). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# A1 (EXACTNESS of the octo shape and its levers on the fused stack, STOP): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-octo3-audit = the audited combined fusion
# arm (fx-all-audit: every integrated lever with its audit) plus QWEN_FAST_OCTO=live, the octo draft, the bundled attention with its audit, the glue levers, the vglue,
# packed-window and F1 audits that compare every native glue site of the octo block with the served path in the trace on every chip, the tile-aligned drafter window with
# its audit, the third block's memory plan, and the host read-back audits SAMPLED (QWEN_FAST_AUDIT_FIRST=1, QWEN_FAST_AUDIT_EVERY=16: the octo-2 audited glue8 attach
# audited two layers of 73 entries after EVERY round and never finished). warmup, coding, parked_turns (the 40 agent turns: returning sessions rebind onto parked engines,
# the tile-aligned window's audit) and concurrent8_steady (the octo rounds). READ: c2_smoke_check clean under every rule at once, i.e. python3 scripts/ci/octo_judge.py
# --container-log <container log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-octo3-audit clean: one "[OCTO] admitted mode=live" line, the UNQUALIFIED
# lines, at least 16 rounds with shape=octo at 8 live and rows=8 (the positive control: written after the octo block's own verify counter moved), no counted m3 round under
# live, no program compiled on the first octo round, the K64j geometry line (extent replay engaged segments=8 flags=0x21 ... G8B1) and the factory line for the bundle's
# launch size (entries=4 kv_share=false), and the lever rules: the octo draft engaged once and serving at least half of the 8-live octo rounds, the bundle engaged ONCE (the
# latch: the warm and the captured fixture build one bundle) with its call line, the glue8 engaged line for every site at users=8 rows=8 and 48 layers, no fallback,
# disabled or fell-back line anywhere. The audits: "tp4 vglue audit <n> exact=True ... sample=first:1,every:16" lines with entries above 0, "[OCTO-ATTN-BUNDLE] audit <n>
# exact=True", the T2 windows and F1 spread audit lines, "tp4 octo glue8" engaged lines and no mismatch; the WP7 audit lines at shape=octo for kv, fold and unfold and the
# WP6 audits of the octo pass (draft_permute_smoke, draft_wp6_smoke); the K/V page writer's "octo 8-row served path" line once; the memory ledger: octo_draft_built and the
# free DRAM after the attach per chip (the audited floor is 3.6 GB after eight engines; RECORD the figure: the third block plus the draft capture are the plan's named
# risk). NO "audit mismatch", no "fell back", no stall. ANY failure is NO-GO for the octo arms and halts the window. Duration (estimate): 90 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-octo3-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,parked_turns,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=120
